\# KigaliFleet — Company Platform Product Requirements Document\
\
\## 1. Product definition\
\
KigaliFleet helps car rental and transport businesses manage their entire operation from one platform.\
\
A registered business should be able to:\
\
\- Manage its vehicles and fleet.\
\- Receive and manage customer bookings.\
\- Manage customers and their documents.\
\- Assign drivers and vehicles.\
\- Manage vehicle handovers and returns.\
\- Track payments, expenses and revenue.\
\- Schedule maintenance.\
\- Manage employees and permissions.\
\- Publish and manage its public storefront.\
\- Communicate with customers.\
\- Understand business performance.\
\- Manage its subscription and account.\
\
The platform should reduce manual administration, prevent operational mistakes, improve customer service and help companies make better business decisions.\
\
\*\*Core promise:\*\* One system to manage the vehicles, people, bookings, money and customers of a transport business.\
\
\## 2. Company types\
\
KigaliFleet should support different types of businesses, not only traditional car rental companies.\
\
\### A. Car rental companies\
\- Self-drive rentals.\
\- Short-term and long-term rentals.\
\- Daily, weekly and monthly rentals.\
\- Vehicle deposits and rental agreements.\
\
\### B. Chauffeur and transport companies\
\- Driver-managed vehicle bookings.\
\- Airport transfers.\
\- Corporate transportation.\
\- Hourly and distance-based transport.\
\
\### C. Tour and travel companies\
\- Tourist transportation.\
\- Multi-day journeys.\
\- Group transportation.\
\- Custom itineraries.\
\
\### D. Fleet operators\
\- Multiple vehicles.\
\- Multiple branches.\
\- Different operational teams.\
\- Fleet utilization and performance tracking.\
\
A business should enable the services it actually provides. KigaliFleet should not force every business to use every module.\
\
\## 3. Company users and roles\
\
A company may have one person doing everything or a team with different responsibilities.\
\
\### Owner\
Full business control:\
\- Business settings.\
\- Employees and permissions.\
\- Vehicles.\
\- Bookings.\
\- Customers.\
\- Finance.\
\- Reports.\
\- Storefront.\
\- Subscription and billing.\
\
\### General manager\
Operational management:\
\- Monitor operations.\
\- Manage bookings.\
\- Assign employees.\
\- Review vehicle availability.\
\- Manage customer issues.\
\- View permitted reports.\
\
\### Dispatcher / Operations officer\
\- View upcoming bookings.\
\- Assign vehicles.\
\- Assign drivers.\
\- Manage pickup and return schedules.\
\- Handle operational changes.\
\- Track active journeys.\
\
\### Accountant / Finance officer\
\- View financial transactions.\
\- Record payments.\
\- Track expenses.\
\- Manage invoices and receipts.\
\- Monitor outstanding balances.\
\- Prepare financial reports.\
\
\### Fleet manager\
\- Manage vehicle records.\
\- Monitor vehicle status.\
\- Schedule maintenance.\
\- Track vehicle documents.\
\- Review vehicle utilization.\
\
\### Mechanic\
\- View assigned maintenance work.\
\- Update repair progress.\
\- Record parts and service costs.\
\- Report completed work.\
\
\### Driver\
\- View assigned trips.\
\- See pickup instructions.\
\- Update trip status.\
\- Report issues.\
\- Submit permitted expense receipts.\
\
\### Front desk / Receptionist\
\- Register customers.\
\- Receive booking requests.\
\- Manage customer communication.\
\- Complete vehicle handovers and returns.\
\
\### Role and permission requirements\
\
Permissions must be configurable and enforced on the backend.\
\
A driver must not automatically see company revenue. A mechanic must not automatically access customer financial records. An accountant should not automatically change fleet maintenance records.\
\
The owner should be able to decide which employees can view, create, edit, approve, delete or export particular records.\
